  "analysis": {
    "boundaries": "Do not merge part_of owners or unknown-overlap owners into one identity; exact graph-equivalent identity is the equality key. Existing locks still apply broader overlap rules. Different properties and prerequisite/preservation old values are not E conflicts. No synonym, partial merge or invented disjointness.",
    "closure_recommendation": "Check actually selected dependency effects jointly before returning whole admission/permission; a parent and selected child can otherwise conflict even if each source node is individually consistent. Final multiple-chosen-root aggregation should use the same invariant if it claims one composed assignment set. This is a design recommendation requiring root scope/implementation approval.",
    "final": "Native final adoption invokes admission/eligibility and whole footprint locks, with no separate typed resolved assignment consistency check found. This reproduction executed admission/permission/core eligibility only; it does not claim a passing complete composed prompt.",
    "minimum_recommendation": "Keep source-local validation, then apply the same E-only typed value/operation/receiver-set invariant after resolving all targets and receiver IDs through exact graph equivalence canonicalization. Different source labels or fixed core-role labels cannot hide the same actual entity assignment.",
    "permission": "permission_scope drops value/type/operation and deduplicates dimension/target/property; actual same-ID collision becomes one footprint row. Explicit alias rows remain two footprints but property locks do not compare values.",
    "resolution": "owner_resolution validates each binding/presence independently; it does not compare resolved E assignments.",
    "source_validation": "_selected_contract keys E assignments by source-local property_key; patch_a and patch_b differ and therefore are not compared."
  },
